node_modules/
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env*.local
# A BARE `.env` IS NOT COVERED BY THE THREE RULES ABOVE — every one of them requires `.local`.
# Nothing writes one today, but a tool (or `vercel env pull`) that did would leave a committable
# file full of secrets. Added 2026-09-10 alongside SUPABASE_PAT.
.env
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log
.vercel
__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/
# Vercel pulled/synced env files — may contain API keys
.env.vercel.*
# Scratch / throwaway work — never commit
scratch/
# Local Claude Code permission prefs — stays on David's machine, never commit
.claude/settings.json
# Personal-financial / personal-sensitive decisions — never commit (family reads the repo)
decisions/PERSONAL-FINANCIAL.local.md

# Generated QR test artifacts — do not clutter root (fixture-picker-shrub-QR.png etc.)
*-QR.png

# TypeScript incremental-build artifacts — never commit
*.tsbuildinfo

# Cost diagnostic scratch output — capture-cost-before.ts writes here so it can never
# clobber the committed proof anchors (BEFORE-NUMBER / AFTER-FLIP snapshots)
docs/cost-to-produce/.scratch/

# Grower-scan named-nursery CSVs — David's competitive analysis of third-party
# nurseries (some are prospects). Desktop-only, NEVER versioned. The recon .md
# notes in this dir ARE tracked (institutional memory about TRACE's own system).
data/grower-scan/*.csv

# Pre-migration database snapshots — NEVER versioned (David's instruction, 2026-09-12).
# `docs/snapshots/pre-*.sql` is a LOGICAL capture taken before a migration is applied, and it
# contains LIVE ROWS: `business_modules` config for every tenant (LAWNS and Test Dave's), plus
# `social_drafts`, `campaigns` and `campaign_posts` contents. Real customer configuration does not
# belong in a git history that outlives the migration it was taken for.
#
# ⚠️ THE ROLLBACK AND THE README ARE CAUGHT BY THIS TOO, AND THAT IS ACCEPTED, NOT OVERLOOKED.
# A narrower `pre-*.sql` rule would version the rollback script — which is pure DDL and safe — but
# it sits beside a file that must never be committed, and a rule that versions one file in a
# secrets-bearing directory is a rule somebody will widen by accident. The whole directory is
# excluded; the rollback's content is reproduced in the close-out ledger row where it is needed.
docs/snapshots/
